WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
A cell holds thousands of proteins, so how do you identify one?

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.880
An enzyme assay tracks activity, and a gel sorts proteins by size.

3
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.800
Neither names the molecule or reads its amino acid sequence.

4
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.640
Mass spectrometry answers by weighing molecules.

5
00:00:21.817 --> 00:00:27.297
Neutral molecules ignore electric fields, so the instrument first adds a charge to

6
00:00:27.297 --> 00:00:32.877
make ions. More charge brings a stronger push, while more mass resists it.

7
00:00:34.037 --> 00:00:38.937
The analyzer sorts ions by mass divided by charge, the mass-to-charge ratio.

8
00:00:40.297 --> 00:00:41.797
Each ratio produces a peak.

9
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.430
One peak is a clue, not always a name.

10
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.350
Suppose two different molecules share the same mass and charge.

11
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.990
Both land on the same peak.

12
00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.650
How can a mass spectrometer still tell them apart?

13
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:04.293
Break them apart and weigh the pieces.

14
00:01:05.653 --> 00:01:10.513
In tandem mass spectrometry, the first stage isolates that peak and shatters its

15
00:01:10.513 --> 00:01:16.273
ions. Different molecules usually split into different fragments, which a second

16
00:01:16.273 --> 00:01:22.853
stage weighs. Weighing charged ions and fragments identifies molecules and reads

17
00:01:22.853 --> 00:01:23.853
protein sequences.

18
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:30.217
To sequence a protein, the enzyme trypsin first cuts it into short peptides.

19
00:01:31.377 --> 00:01:36.137
The first stage selects one peptide ion and breaks it into a ladder of fragments,

20
00:01:36.797 --> 00:01:38.617
each one amino acid shorter.

21
00:01:40.017 --> 00:01:43.797
Subtracting neighbouring masses names each amino acid in order.

22
00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:47.617
Two amino acids weigh exactly the same, though.

23
00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.070
Crowded samples can hide scarce targets.

24
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.730
Fasting blood holds insulin at a few tens of picomolar.

25
00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:01.570
Albumin outnumbers it roughly ten million to one, enough to drown its signal.

26
00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:07.750
So liquid chromatography separates the mixture first, feeding compounds in over

27
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:08.750
time.

28
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:10.903
A missing peak needs caution.

29
00:02:12.263 --> 00:02:16.743
Every instrument has a detection limit, the lowest level it can reliably see.

30
00:02:18.003 --> 00:02:22.663
Not detected means below that floor, not zero, so studies report their limits.

31
00:02:24.223 --> 00:02:28.223
Strong claims also check whether two methods that fail differently agree.

32
00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:31.007
The same care tracks drugs.

33
00:02:32.547 --> 00:02:36.827
Male mice received the drug isoguvacine, 20 mg/kg.

34
00:02:38.207 --> 00:02:43.007
Liquid chromatography–mass spectrometry then detected it in blood and liver.

35
00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:47.587
It was not detected in brain or cerebrospinal fluid.

36
00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:54.807
Detection limits were 640 picomolar in fluids and 16 nanomolar in tissue.

37
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.680
Tandem mass spectrometry also serves newborn screening.

38
00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:08.660
MCAD deficiency, a missing fat-burning enzyme, affects roughly 1 in 10,000 to 20,000

39
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:14.000
births. A heel prick read by tandem mass spectrometry catches most cases.

40
00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.600
A few babies still fall ill before the result is back.

41
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:24.120
Heavy nitrogen weighs more than normal nitrogen, so weighing tracks it.

42
00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:30.400
In the 1930s, Rudolf Schoenheimer fed rats nitrogen-labeled amino acids.

43
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:36.600
The heavy tag entered proteins throughout the body, showing "the dynamic state of

44
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.600
body constituents."

45
00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:43.300
Ion and fragment mass turns hidden mixtures into names and sequences.
